From: TinyUSB backport: PR #2937 + commit 4bfba6b + ISO ZLP fix
Subject: rp2040: three ISO transfer fixes for UAC2 streaming on pico-sdk 0.18.0

Fix 1 (PR #2937, 2025-03-07 — dcd_rp2040.c):
  dcd_edpt_iso_activate() did not abort an in-flight ISO transfer before
  re-enabling the endpoint on SET_INTERFACE → panic "ep already available".

Fix 2 (commit 4bfba6b, 2025-08-05 — dcd_rp2040.c):
  hw_handle_buff_status() notified the stack before resetting ep->active.
  Audio class queues next ISO from xfer-complete callback → panic.

Fix 3 (new — rp2040_usb.c):
  RP2040 fires buf_status for ISO IN on every SOF including ZLP frames.
  After fix #2 resets ep->active, the next SOF hits inactive ISO.
  Returning true would post a spurious event causing double-start (AVAIL
  already set) → panic. Return false to silently ignore ZLP SOF interrupts;
  the real event already queued handles the reload.

Upstream: https://github.com/hathach/tinyusb/pull/2937
          https://github.com/hathach/tinyusb/commit/4bfba6b09a90d5321b3dbd2d986760438417c430

